# The store is committed markdown and the suite reads it back byte for byte, so the working
# tree has to hold the bytes the repository holds on every platform. Without this file a
# Windows clone under Git for Windows' installer default, core.autocrlf=true, checks
# `.work/items/*.md` out as CRLF: measured on the 2026-09-07 cross-platform run, every shard
# then read as an `H16` finding, `documented-numbers.test.ts` counted 0 records under
# `.work/items`, and the human-layout snapshot differed by a trailing `\r` on every line.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than `text=auto` alone, because `text=auto` normalises what is committed and
# still lets the checkout follow `core.autocrlf`. This is the checkout half.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything below is a byte stream: a checkout must not touch it whatever its extension
# suggests to git's own heuristics.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.tgz binary
